WEBVTT

00:02.438 --> 00:04.564
Water.

00:04.774 --> 00:06.149
Earth.

00:06.776 --> 00:08.610
Fire.

00:08.945 --> 00:10.529
Air.

00:10.697 --> 00:14.700
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:14.826 --> 00:18.954
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.664 --> 00:22.457
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.625 --> 00:23.917
could stop them.

00:24.043 --> 00:25.627
But when the world needed him most,

00:25.753 --> 00:27.212
he vanished.

00:27.338 --> 00:29.256
100 years passed, and my brother and I

00:29.382 --> 00:32.676
discovered the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.094 --> 00:34.845
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:35.054 --> 00:37.639
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.724 --> 00:38.724
Unh!

00:38.808 --> 00:41.977
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:01.039 --> 01:03.498
Um, aren't you forgetting the tarp?

01:03.624 --> 01:05.375
Right. Got it.

01:05.877 --> 01:07.878
Sokka, you're supposed to put the tarp

01:07.962 --> 01:09.046
on top of the tent.

01:09.130 --> 01:10.881
You know, so we don't get rained on?

01:11.341 --> 01:12.841
Ordinarily, you'd be right,

01:12.925 --> 01:14.217
but seeing how it's the dry season,

01:14.302 --> 01:15.302
you're not.

01:15.511 --> 01:17.054
Besides, that tarp makes
a pretty warm blanket.

01:17.138 --> 01:18.638
But what if it does rain?

01:18.765 --> 01:19.848
What if it doesn't?

01:19.974 --> 01:21.683
Then I would have put
the tarp up for nothing.

01:21.809 --> 01:24.353
You're infuriating.

01:24.479 --> 01:26.646
Katara, why don't you worry about
gathering the firewood?

01:26.773 --> 01:30.150
Because that kindling's
looking pretty sorry.

01:30.276 --> 01:32.069
If you don't like my firewood--

01:33.654 --> 01:36.281
Fine by me! If you're not
gonna do your job--

01:37.700 --> 01:39.785
Okay, I got the grub
if you guys got the...

01:39.911 --> 01:41.495
Hey, where's the campfire,

01:41.621 --> 01:43.080
and what happened to the tent?

01:43.206 --> 01:46.041
Why don't you ask
Miss Know-it-all, Queen of the twigs?

01:46.167 --> 01:50.253
Yeah? Well,
you're Mr. Lazy-bum, King of the...

01:50.380 --> 01:51.588
Tents!

01:52.882 --> 01:54.591
Okay. Listen, guys.

01:54.717 --> 01:56.635
Harsh words won't solve problems.

01:56.761 --> 01:57.844
Action will.

01:57.970 --> 01:59.888
Why don't you just switch jobs?

02:00.014 --> 02:01.139
-Sounds good.
-Whatever.

02:01.224 --> 02:02.224
You see that?

02:02.392 --> 02:04.351
Settling feuds and making peace...

02:04.477 --> 02:06.645
All in a day's work for the Avatar.

02:22.495 --> 02:24.454
Come on, Momo. That's fair.

02:24.789 --> 02:26.456
Appa's got five stomachs.

02:30.962 --> 02:33.755
There it is, guys, The Great Divide.

02:33.881 --> 02:36.716
Wow. I could just stare at it forever.

02:36.843 --> 02:38.593
Okay. I've seen enough.

02:38.719 --> 02:41.304
How can you not be fascinated, Sokka?

02:41.431 --> 02:44.015
This is the largest canyon
in the entire world.

02:44.142 --> 02:46.393
Then I'm sure we'll be
able to see it very clearly

02:46.519 --> 02:48.019
from the air while we fly away.

02:48.146 --> 02:49.604
Hey, if you're looking
for the canyon guide,

02:49.689 --> 02:51.022
I was here first.

02:51.399 --> 02:54.484
Ooh. Canyon guide. Sounds informative.

02:54.610 --> 02:56.653
Believe me, he's more
than a tour guide.

02:56.779 --> 02:57.821
He's an earthbender,

02:57.947 --> 02:59.489
and the only way
in and out of the canyon

02:59.615 --> 03:00.991
is with his help.

03:01.117 --> 03:03.243
And he's taking my tribe across next.

03:03.369 --> 03:05.120
Calm down. We know you're next.

03:05.246 --> 03:07.581
You wouldn't be calm if the
Fire Nation destroyed your home

03:07.707 --> 03:08.999
and forced you to flee.

03:09.208 --> 03:11.168
My whole tribe has to
walk thousands of miles

03:11.252 --> 03:13.795
to the capital city of Ba Sing Se.

03:14.088 --> 03:15.505
You're a refugee.

03:15.673 --> 03:17.257
Tell me something I don't know.

03:20.219 --> 03:21.678
Is that your tribe?

03:21.804 --> 03:23.138
It most certainly is not.

03:23.264 --> 03:24.931
That's the Zhang tribe,

03:25.057 --> 03:26.725
a bunch of lowlife thieves.

03:26.851 --> 03:28.185
They've been the enemies

03:28.311 --> 03:29.603
of my tribe for a hundred years.

03:30.855 --> 03:31.980
Hey, Zhangs!

03:32.106 --> 03:33.857
I'm saving a spot for my tribe,

03:33.983 --> 03:35.525
so don't even think of stealing it.

03:35.735 --> 03:37.652
Where are the rest of the Gan Jin?

03:37.945 --> 03:40.572
Still tidying up their campsite?

03:40.698 --> 03:43.492
Yes, but they sent me
ahead of them to hold a spot.

03:43.868 --> 03:45.827
I didn't know the canyon guide
took reservations.

03:46.120 --> 03:47.787
Of course you didn't.

03:47.914 --> 03:49.331
That's the ignorance I'd expect

03:49.457 --> 03:51.208
from a messy Zhang,

03:51.292 --> 03:53.502
so unorganized
and ill-prepared for a journey.

04:04.764 --> 04:07.182
Sorry about the wait, youngsters.

04:07.308 --> 04:10.143
Who's ready to cross this here canyon?

04:10.269 --> 04:12.771
One of them, I think.

04:12.897 --> 04:14.856
I was here first.
My party's on their way.

04:15.107 --> 04:17.609
I can't guide people who aren't here.

04:18.027 --> 04:20.612
Guess you guys will have
to make the trip tomorrow.

04:22.406 --> 04:23.448
Wait! Here they come.

04:30.456 --> 04:31.706
You're not seriously gonna cave in

04:31.832 --> 04:33.291
to these spoiled Gan Jins.

04:33.417 --> 04:35.502
I mean, we're refugees, too,

04:35.628 --> 04:37.712
and we've got sick people
that need shelter.

04:37.838 --> 04:39.589
I, well...

04:40.007 --> 04:42.384
We've got old people
who are weary from traveling.

04:42.760 --> 04:45.095
Sick people get
priority over old people.

04:45.263 --> 04:47.597
Maybe you Zhangs wouldn't
have so many sick people

04:47.723 --> 04:49.933
if you weren't such slobs.

04:50.226 --> 04:52.269
If you Gan Jins weren't so clean,

04:52.395 --> 04:54.729
maybe you wouldn't live to be so old.

04:54.814 --> 04:56.022
I could smell your stink...

04:56.107 --> 04:57.440
Well, Aang, ready to put

04:57.525 --> 04:58.775
your peacemaking skills to the test?

04:58.901 --> 05:00.694
I don't know...

05:00.820 --> 05:02.571
A fight over chores is one thing.

05:02.697 --> 05:05.365
These people have been
feuding for a hundred years.

05:05.491 --> 05:07.409
Everyone listen up!

05:07.535 --> 05:09.119
This is the Avatar,

05:09.245 --> 05:10.704
and if you give him a chance,

05:10.830 --> 05:12.539
I'm sure he can come up
with a compromise

05:12.665 --> 05:14.457
that will make everyone happy.

05:16.544 --> 05:20.046
You could share the earthbender
and travel together?

05:20.381 --> 05:22.924
Absolutely not. We'd rather
be taken by the Fire Nation

05:23.050 --> 05:25.510
than travel with those
stinking thieves.

05:26.053 --> 05:28.388
We wouldn't travel
with you pompous fools anyway.

05:30.308 --> 05:31.474
All right, here's the deal!

05:31.559 --> 05:33.101
You're all going down together,

05:33.185 --> 05:35.687
and Appa here
will fly your sick and elderly across.

05:35.855 --> 05:37.314
Does that seem fair?

05:48.075 --> 05:50.869
Sorry, Appa. You'll have to
do this on your own.

05:50.953 --> 05:53.705
Aang, this feuding tribe
stuff is serious business.

05:53.998 --> 05:55.832
Are you sure it's a good idea
getting involved in this?

05:56.000 --> 05:58.960
To tell the truth, I'm not sure,

05:59.086 --> 06:00.295
but when have I ever been?

06:00.504 --> 06:01.838
He's the avatar, Sokka.

06:02.256 --> 06:04.257
Making peace
between people is his job.

06:04.634 --> 06:07.385
His job's gonna make us cross this
whole thing on foot, isn't it?

06:07.845 --> 06:10.180
Okay, now comes the bad news.

06:10.514 --> 06:13.183
No food allowed in the canyon.

06:13.309 --> 06:17.187
It attracts dangerous predators.

06:17.521 --> 06:19.606
No food? This is ridiculous.

06:19.732 --> 06:24.069
You babies can go
a day without food.

06:24.612 --> 06:27.280
Would you rather be hungry or dead?

06:28.199 --> 06:30.533
Now, we're heading down in 10 minutes.

06:30.618 --> 06:32.744
All food better be in your gut,

06:32.995 --> 06:34.287
or in the garbage!

06:41.128 --> 06:44.005
Appa's gonna take good care of you
till we get there.

06:44.548 --> 06:46.132
See you on the other side, buddy.

06:46.258 --> 06:47.342
Yip yip!

07:02.024 --> 07:03.400
Nice bending.

07:04.235 --> 07:07.195
The job's much more than bending, kid.

07:07.321 --> 07:08.822
Folks want information.

07:10.241 --> 07:12.450
Many of you are probably wondering

07:12.576 --> 07:14.411
how canyons are formed.

07:14.537 --> 07:16.955
Experts tell us
this canyon was most likely

07:17.039 --> 07:20.125
carved into the ground
by earth spirits,

07:20.209 --> 07:22.794
who were angry at local farmers

07:22.878 --> 07:26.339
for not offering them
a proper sacrifice.

07:33.222 --> 07:37.517
Ha ha!
Guess the spirits are still angry.

07:37.935 --> 07:40.562
Hope you all brought sacrifices.

07:45.401 --> 07:48.945
Okay. Everyone
stand clear of the wall.

07:54.618 --> 07:55.785
Why did you do that?

07:55.911 --> 07:59.080
These people are fleeing
the Fire Nation, aren't they?

07:59.206 --> 08:01.708
I've got to make sure
we can't be followed.

08:01.834 --> 08:03.543
We'll be safe now.

08:08.632 --> 08:10.049
We've got to help him!!

08:11.594 --> 08:12.761
Aah!

08:15.431 --> 08:17.140
Okay, now we've got to help me!

08:22.229 --> 08:23.521
Aah!

08:23.606 --> 08:24.606
Hah!

08:37.912 --> 08:38.995
What was that?

08:39.121 --> 08:40.705
Canyon crawler.

08:40.831 --> 08:44.209
And there's sure to be more.

08:44.376 --> 08:46.795
Your arms... They're broken.

08:46.879 --> 08:49.422
Without my arms, I got no bending.

08:49.632 --> 08:50.799
In other words...

08:50.883 --> 08:52.509
We're trapped in this canyon.

09:03.521 --> 09:05.271
I thought the whole point
of ditching our food

09:05.397 --> 09:08.191
was so we wouldn't have to deal
with things like canyon crawlers.

09:08.317 --> 09:09.442
It's the Zhangs.

09:09.527 --> 09:12.946
They took food down here
even after the guide told them not to.

09:13.322 --> 09:14.614
What?

09:14.698 --> 09:16.491
If there's anyone who
can't go without food for a day,

09:16.575 --> 09:18.868
it's these pampered Gan Jins.

09:19.453 --> 09:20.620
I hope you're happy.

09:20.704 --> 09:22.872
We're stuck in this canyon
with no way out.

09:23.123 --> 09:25.542
Why don't you thank yourself,
food-hider?

09:25.626 --> 09:28.127
Look, sticking together
is the only way to--

09:28.212 --> 09:30.713
I'm not walking another step
with the likes of them.

09:30.798 --> 09:33.258
Now there's something we can agree on.

09:33.843 --> 09:34.968
Any ideas?

09:35.219 --> 09:38.137
No bending. We need to get
out of this canyon.

09:38.222 --> 09:40.098
I won't die down here.

09:40.182 --> 09:43.017
I won't become part of the food chain.

09:44.019 --> 09:45.895
See? We're going to become
part of the food chain

09:45.980 --> 09:47.146
because of you.

09:47.565 --> 09:50.567
Sure. Unjustly blame
the Zhangs, like you always do.

09:50.818 --> 09:52.110
Gladly.

09:52.236 --> 09:53.361
Enough!

09:53.487 --> 09:55.154
I thought I could
help you guys get along,

09:55.281 --> 09:56.531
but I guess that's not gonna happen.

09:59.243 --> 10:00.451
We should split up--

10:00.536 --> 10:03.246
Gan Jins on this side
and Zhangs on that side.

10:03.706 --> 10:05.456
We'll travel in two separate lines.

10:12.464 --> 10:14.132
Sokka, you go with the Zhangs,

10:14.258 --> 10:15.842
and, Katara, you go with the Gan Jins.

10:16.343 --> 10:19.387
See if you can find out why
they hate each other so much.

10:38.073 --> 10:40.158
So, you guys aren't gonna
put up your tarps?

10:40.326 --> 10:42.327
What for? It's the dry season.

10:42.411 --> 10:43.620
Exactly!

10:43.954 --> 10:46.456
Besides, we like to use
the tarp as a blanket.

10:46.832 --> 10:48.374
Finally someone gets it.

10:56.216 --> 10:57.675
Do you really think it'll rain?

10:57.968 --> 11:01.179
No, but you can never
be too careful, right?

11:19.990 --> 11:21.991
Would you care for some bread, Katara?

11:22.076 --> 11:23.910
So it was you guys who had food.

11:24.244 --> 11:25.370
Come now.

11:25.454 --> 11:26.829
Do you really think
that tribe of thieves

11:26.914 --> 11:28.206
isn't smuggling food?

11:28.290 --> 11:30.083
Why should my people go hungry

11:30.167 --> 11:33.211
when the sneaky Zhangs
are stuffing their faces?

11:33.837 --> 11:37.757
Well, I guess it's okay
if everyone's doing it.

11:41.595 --> 11:44.722
So, why does your tribe
hate the Zhangs so much?

11:45.099 --> 11:47.600
You seem like a smart girl, Katara.

11:47.685 --> 11:50.311
I bet you would enjoy
hearing some history.

11:57.319 --> 11:59.821
The patriarch
of our tribe, Jin Wei,

11:59.947 --> 12:01.447
was an earthbender warrior

12:01.573 --> 12:03.825
who was assigned an important duty:

12:03.951 --> 12:06.119
Transporting our sacred orb

12:06.245 --> 12:09.831
From the great eastern gate
to the great western gate.

12:15.129 --> 12:17.046
Taking the orb
from the east to the west

12:17.172 --> 12:20.341
represents the sun's
rising and setting.

12:20.467 --> 12:24.637
It was our tribe's
ancient redemption ritual.

12:24.763 --> 12:26.639
But as he approached the gate,

12:26.765 --> 12:29.934
Jin Wei was attacked
by one of the Zhangs--

12:30.060 --> 12:32.186
A vermin named Wei Jin

12:32.312 --> 12:35.314
who looked at the orb with envy.

12:35.441 --> 12:39.027
That coward Wei Jin
knocked Jin Wei to the ground

12:39.153 --> 12:41.154
and stole our sacred orb.

12:42.823 --> 12:45.324
Our people have never forgotten.

12:45.451 --> 12:48.036
You can never trust a Zhang.

12:54.084 --> 12:55.376
Care for some meat?

12:55.502 --> 12:56.878
Would I?

12:57.212 --> 12:58.921
I know what you must be thinking.

12:59.006 --> 13:00.882
We're horrible for
endangering everybody

13:01.008 --> 13:02.383
by bringing food down here.

13:03.802 --> 13:05.636
The Gan Jins think so badly of us,

13:05.763 --> 13:07.722
they probably assumed
we brought food in

13:07.848 --> 13:09.682
and decided to bring
food in themselves.

13:09.808 --> 13:11.309
That's why we brought food in.

13:12.561 --> 13:14.145
Our conflict with the Gan Jin

13:14.271 --> 13:16.689
goes back over 100 years.

13:21.028 --> 13:23.696
Our forefather, Wei Jin,
was leaving the western gate

13:23.822 --> 13:26.991
of our village when he saw
a figure in the distance.

13:27.117 --> 13:30.870
It was a man of the Gan Jin tribe,
Jin Wei,

13:30.996 --> 13:32.747
collapsed on the ground.

13:32.873 --> 13:34.999
Noble Wei Jin stopped to help him.

13:35.125 --> 13:38.044
Jin Wei was transporting a sacred orb,

13:38.128 --> 13:41.964
a very powerful relic used in
his tribe's redemption ritual.

13:42.466 --> 13:44.550
Wei Jin tried to tend
to the man's wounds,

13:44.635 --> 13:47.845
but Jin Wei insisted the orb
was more important

13:47.930 --> 13:50.640
and asked him to take it
back to his tribe.

13:50.724 --> 13:53.643
Kind Wei Jin promised to send
help for the man

13:53.727 --> 13:54.894
as soon as he could.

13:55.145 --> 13:57.146
But as Wei Jin crossed the border

13:57.231 --> 13:59.148
to return the orb
into Gan Jin territory,

13:59.233 --> 14:00.733
he was arrested.

14:05.572 --> 14:08.825
Instead of thanking him
for his kind and selfless deed,

14:08.951 --> 14:11.994
they sentenced him
to 20 long years in prison.

14:13.789 --> 14:16.332
We Zhangs will never forget
that injustice.

14:16.834 --> 14:18.584
That's just terrible.

14:18.794 --> 14:19.877
Are you gonna finish that?

14:22.172 --> 14:23.339
Sure would be nice

14:23.423 --> 14:25.424
to be around one of those campfires.

14:25.551 --> 14:27.844
Telling stories and laughing.

14:28.470 --> 14:31.722
It's okay, Momo.
We'll be out of here soon enough,

14:31.849 --> 14:33.808
and then we can eat our weight
in litchi nuts.

14:40.149 --> 14:42.817
Nah. I'll wait for the litchi nuts.

14:43.152 --> 14:46.779
It's lonely,
isn't it, being impartial?

14:47.406 --> 14:49.407
I wish I could help
these people get along,

14:49.491 --> 14:51.284
but it just seems impossible.

14:51.410 --> 14:52.827
Anyhow, I guess our biggest problem

14:52.911 --> 14:54.036
Is getting out of here.

14:54.246 --> 14:58.583
I'm not so sure the two problems
are unrelated.

15:05.924 --> 15:09.051
All clear.
We're almost to the other side.

15:19.646 --> 15:21.898
Katara, Sokka,
will these people cooperate

15:21.982 --> 15:23.482
long enough to get out of the canyon?

15:23.650 --> 15:24.859
I don't think so, Aang.

15:24.943 --> 15:27.195
The Zhangs really
wronged the Gan Jins.

15:27.321 --> 15:30.156
They ambushed Jin Wei
and stole the sacred orb.

15:30.532 --> 15:31.741
What are you talking about?

15:32.034 --> 15:33.993
Yeah, Katara, what
are you talking about?

15:34.161 --> 15:36.120
Wei Jin didn't steal the orb.

15:36.330 --> 15:37.872
He was returning it
to their village gate

15:37.956 --> 15:39.749
and was wrongfully
punished by the Gan Jin.

15:40.000 --> 15:41.792
Not punished enough, if you ask me.

15:42.211 --> 15:44.962
Okay, okay. I get it.
Now I need your help.

15:45.088 --> 15:47.548
Let's get everyone together
at the base of the canyon wall.

15:56.141 --> 15:58.476
Please, everyone.
As soon as we get out of here,

15:58.560 --> 16:00.311
we can eat and then
go our separate ways.

16:00.604 --> 16:02.146
But I need you all
to put your heads together

16:02.231 --> 16:04.023
and figure out a way up this cliff.

16:04.316 --> 16:06.150
Maybe the Zhang can climb the wall

16:06.276 --> 16:08.444
With their long,
disgusting fingernails.

16:08.528 --> 16:11.364
Sorry.
I forgot that to the Gan Jin,

16:11.448 --> 16:15.493
unclipped fingernails is a crime
punishable by 20 years in jail.

16:15.661 --> 16:17.119
Why, you dirty thief.

16:17.246 --> 16:18.996
You pompous fool.

16:21.291 --> 16:22.750
Guys, focus!

16:22.834 --> 16:24.543
How many times do I have to say it?

16:24.670 --> 16:26.295
Harsh words won't solve problems.

16:26.463 --> 16:27.755
Action will!

16:28.715 --> 16:30.841
Perhaps the Avatar is right.

16:31.260 --> 16:32.802
Yes. Perhaps he is.

16:35.264 --> 16:37.848
Harsh words will never
solve our problems.

16:38.141 --> 16:39.934
Action will.

16:43.272 --> 16:44.355
Aah!

16:48.735 --> 16:52.280
To the death, and let this
be the end of this rivalry.

16:52.698 --> 16:54.282
You know, I take it back.

16:54.366 --> 16:55.825
Harsh words aren't so bad.

17:12.009 --> 17:13.551
Hyah!

17:21.601 --> 17:23.477
Is that food?

17:23.937 --> 17:25.730
Everyone smuggled food down here?

17:25.856 --> 17:27.189
Unbelievable!

17:27.316 --> 17:28.774
You guys put our lives in danger

17:28.900 --> 17:31.152
because you couldn't go
without a snack for a day?

17:31.403 --> 17:34.113
You are all awful!

17:41.079 --> 17:42.872
So hungry...

17:42.998 --> 17:46.334
Is that egg custard in that tart?

17:55.552 --> 17:58.763
No.
That's a lot of canyon crawlers.

17:58.889 --> 18:00.723
We barely survived one.

18:00.849 --> 18:02.767
They're coming back for me.

18:02.893 --> 18:05.728
They've had a taste,
and they're coming back for me.

18:05.854 --> 18:06.979
Sokka, wait.

18:07.105 --> 18:09.565
I don't care about the stupid feud.

18:09.691 --> 18:11.484
I just want us to get
out of here alive.

18:11.651 --> 18:14.987
Me, too. I only took their side
because they fed me.

18:20.744 --> 18:35.674
Hyah!

18:48.063 --> 18:49.105
Aah!

18:54.277 --> 18:55.277
Aah!

19:16.591 --> 19:20.094
Everybody, watch me and do what I do!

19:46.830 --> 19:48.247
Now follow me.

19:48.373 --> 19:49.999
We're riding out of this hole.

20:06.933 --> 20:08.684
Everyone get off!

20:13.148 --> 20:14.190
We made it!

20:27.245 --> 20:29.872
I never thought a Gan Jin
could get his hands dirty like that.

20:30.373 --> 20:33.375
And I never knew you Zhangs
were so reliable in a pinch.

20:33.960 --> 20:36.003
Perhaps we're not
so different after all.

20:37.964 --> 20:40.007
Too bad we can't rewrite history.

20:40.091 --> 20:43.761
You thieves stole our sacred orb
from Jin Wei.

20:44.221 --> 20:48.516
You tyrants unjustly imprisoned
Wei Jin for 20 long years.

20:48.975 --> 20:51.310
Wait a second...

20:51.686 --> 20:55.356
Jin Wei? Wei Jin? I know those guys.

20:55.732 --> 20:58.526
Yes, yes.
We're all aware of the story.

20:58.777 --> 21:01.278
No, I mean I really knew them.

21:01.404 --> 21:04.156
I might not look it,
but I'm 112 years old.

21:04.282 --> 21:05.824
I was there 100 years ago

21:05.909 --> 21:07.618
on the day you're talking about.

21:08.578 --> 21:10.996
There seems to be a lot of confusion
about what happened.

21:11.081 --> 21:14.375
First of all, Jin Wei
and Wei Jin weren't enemies.

21:14.543 --> 21:17.378
They were brothers. Twins, in fact.

21:17.671 --> 21:20.422
And they were eight,
and most importantly,

21:20.715 --> 21:22.091
they were just playing a game.

21:23.343 --> 21:24.802
The sacred orb from the legend--

21:24.928 --> 21:26.053
That was the ball.

21:26.179 --> 21:27.596
And the eastern and western gates

21:27.681 --> 21:28.931
were the goal posts.

21:29.307 --> 21:31.183
Jin Wei had the ball
and was running toward the goal

21:31.268 --> 21:32.977
when he fell and fumbled it.

21:33.353 --> 21:35.187
Wei Jin didn't steal the ball.

21:35.272 --> 21:36.939
He picked it up and started
running it back

21:37.107 --> 21:39.775
toward the other goal,
but he stepped out of bounds.

21:41.069 --> 21:42.945
So the official put him
in the penalty box--

21:43.029 --> 21:45.656
Not for 20 long years
but for two short minutes.

21:45.782 --> 21:47.032
Hee hee hee!

21:47.659 --> 21:50.411
There was no stealing
and no putting anyone in prison...

21:50.537 --> 21:51.870
Just a game.

21:52.372 --> 21:54.915
You're saying the sacred orb
was actually a sacred ball?

21:55.083 --> 21:56.959
Nope, just a regular ball.

21:57.335 --> 21:59.211
What about our tribe's
redemption ritual?

21:59.337 --> 22:01.714
That's what the game
was called, Redemption.

22:02.173 --> 22:04.758
As soon as someone got
the ball from one goal to the other,

22:04.843 --> 22:07.136
everyone would yell, "Redemption!"

22:09.139 --> 22:11.140
Don't get me wrong...
Wei Jin was kind of a slob,

22:11.224 --> 22:12.641
and Jin Wei was a little stuffy.

22:12.726 --> 22:13.851
That much is true.

22:14.477 --> 22:16.562
But they respected
each other's differences

22:16.646 --> 22:18.272
enough to share
the same playing field.

22:19.024 --> 22:21.191
I suppose it's time
we forget the past.

22:22.110 --> 22:23.819
And look to the future.

22:32.871 --> 22:35.914
Good to see you, boy.
Did you miss me?

22:36.291 --> 22:38.292
I cannot thank you enough, Avatar.

22:38.752 --> 22:40.544
Well, you know. I try.

22:43.423 --> 22:45.799
Let us travel
to the Earth Kingdom capital

22:45.884 --> 22:47.551
as one tribe.

22:49.512 --> 22:50.846
I'm going, too!

22:50.930 --> 22:52.514
I'm sick of this place.

22:53.516 --> 22:55.517
That's some luck
you knew Jin Wei and Wei Jin.

22:55.935 --> 22:57.603
You could call it luck,

22:57.854 --> 22:59.229
or you could call it lying.

22:59.314 --> 23:01.482
-What?
-I made the whole thing up.

23:02.025 --> 23:03.817
You did not.

23:04.110 --> 23:05.611
That is so wrong.

23:05.945 --> 23:07.613
Now, where's that custard tart?

23:08.031 --> 23:09.031
I'm starving!
